    field unitSelectorGacha type="[UnitSelectorGachaMst]" {
        key "JukkSeNA"
        doc """
        The Unit Selector catalogue (UnitSelectorGachaMstResponse).  Loaded at
        boot and, until 2026-09-13, never sent -- which is the OTHER half of
        "selector summons are not working".

        SummonsDetailScene::initSummontickets @0x1D8E304 builds the scene's
        selected-selector list by walking UnitSelectorGachaMstList for rows
        whose gacha_gate_id is the open gate, and touchBegan @0x16A73FC sends
        the player to the unit picker only when that list is NOT empty.  With
        the catalogue absent the list can never fill, so SUMMON on a selector
        gate fell through to the ordinary paid pull.  SummonsScrlItem::addObject
        @0x16D9F70 reads the same list for the ticket count on the rail tile,
        and UnitSelectorGachaUnitSelectScene::initialize @0x1D95CCC reads it for
        the grid of units to choose from.

        readParam @0x1CCAD3C merges rather than replaces (addObject with no
        remove), and rows are keyed by ticket id, so re-sending is harmless.
        """
    }
